test file.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012XowJVZj4c1G92gnMJ4PjY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015fCmVVnBM6QnhjMdZAeScC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BaLdiJGEjJgHPi2YKeusHD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both correct under half-even. I'll create the branch and make the change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NvJSnLYmqR7tcgvxsJDSny", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019HmrnUbVQTPYe9CQVF8iDn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The change is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0134MDTkqgW7ec8wtR5VSajs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0186b9Xfv9rsHxEUDWgRTKM4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging to main requires code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YAaJjJQQgwDe6i8Np1PfQK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 specifies banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which the function's docstring already describes. This switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nChecked by hand against the test cases:\n- 2.675 -> 2.68 (7 is odd, so round up to even)\n- 2.665 -> 2.66 (6 is even, so keep)\n\nCI on 08d3cd5986: passed (ci-0001).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YRocxn4ACcKyZH6T8tTYfC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created (#101), but the reviewer list is empty because the request timed out partway. I'll add alex as reviewer on #101 rather than open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UYik1qHexcNqvJPyvid5T8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Change:** `src/money.py` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`, which matches FIN-212 and the function's docstring. The commit is on branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding` (sha `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** the first attempt to open the PR timed out. Checking open PRs showed #101 had been created, but with no reviewers, so I added alex to it instead of opening a second PR.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so it still needs that approval before it can land.", "type": "text"}]}]}